# Hindi Language Learning Notes — Casual Talk & Everyday Sentences

> **Pronunciation Guide Key:**
> - **aa** = long "a" (as in "father")
> - **a** = short "a" (as in "about")
> - **ee** = long "i" (as in "see")
> - **i** = short "i" (as in "sit")
> - **oo** = long "u" (as in "moon")
> - **u** = short "u" (as in "put")
> - **ai** = as in "bet"
> - **au** = as in "caught")
> - **th** = soft "t" with breath (NOT English "th")
> - **dh** = soft "d" with breath
> - **ch** = as in "church"
> - **sh** = as in "ship"
> - **bh** = "b" with breath
> - **kh** = "k" with breath
> - **gh** = "g" with breath
> - **ph** = "p" with breath (NOT "f")
> - **ṛ** / **r** = rolled tongue "r"
> - **ñ** = nasal "n" (as in "ankle")

